``` password-spray-4625 v2 - PENDING VALIDATION ```
``` Not yet run against live data. query.spl remains the validated detection. ```
```
Fixes a window-alignment evasion in query.spl.

v1 groups events with `bucket _time span=10m`, which cuts time into fixed
10-minute blocks aligned to the clock (10:00-10:10, 10:10-10:20, ...). A
spray that crosses a block edge is split in two. For example, 5 users
failing at 10:07-10:09 and 5 more at 10:11-10:13 is 10 users in 6 minutes,
but each block sees only 5, so neither reaches distinct_users >= 6 and
nothing fires. An attacker doesn't need to know where the edges are:
pacing the spray at about 5 users per 10 minutes stays under the threshold
in every block.

v2 uses a sliding 10-minute window per source (streamstats time_window),
so the thresholds are tested against the previous 10 minutes as of every
event rather than against fixed clock blocks. It then returns one row per
spraying source covering all of that source's failures in the search range,
so the analyst sees the whole spray rather than one slice of it.

Thresholds and severity bands are unchanged from v1.

Operational note: streamstats time_window is limited by max_stream_window
in limits.conf (default 10000 events per window). A source generating more
failures than that in 10 minutes will already be obvious, but the limit is
worth knowing.

Reproduce with ../../validation/hec_scenarios.py (scenarios spray-control,
spray-boundary).
```
index=* (sourcetype=WinEventLog:Security OR sourcetype=XmlWinEventLog:Security OR sourcetype=*wineventlog*security*)
EventCode=4625
| eval src_ip=coalesce(src_ip, Source_Network_Address, SourceNetworkAddress, IpAddress, ip, ClientIP)
| eval user=lower(coalesce(user, TargetUserName, Account_Name, Target_Account, TargetUser, UserName))
| eval host=coalesce(dest, ComputerName, host)
| where isnotnull(src_ip) AND src_ip!="-"
``` time_window requires time-ordered events ```
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m
    count as failures_10m
    dc(user) as distinct_users_10m
    dc(host) as distinct_hosts_10m
  by src_ip
| eval spray_hit=if(failures_10m>=8 AND distinct_users_10m>=6, 1, 0)
``` keep every event from a source that crossed the threshold at any point ```
| eventstats max(spray_hit) as src_is_spraying by src_ip
| where src_is_spraying=1
| stats
    min(_time) as first_seen
    max(_time) as last_seen
    count as total_failures
    max(distinct_users_10m) as peak_distinct_users_10m
    max(distinct_hosts_10m) as peak_distinct_hosts_10m
    values(user) as users_sample
    values(host) as hosts_sample
  by src_ip
| eval detection="password-spray-4625"
| eval severity=case(peak_distinct_users_10m>=12 OR peak_distinct_hosts_10m>=3, "high", peak_distinct_users_10m>=8, "medium", true(), "low")
| sort 0 - last_seen
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| table first_seen last_seen src_ip total_failures peak_distinct_users_10m peak_distinct_hosts_10m severity users_sample hosts_sample detection
